tidal_download
==============

Auth, metadata and stream resolution are provided by python-tidal (tidalapi),
an actively maintained third-party library, installed as a normal dependency.

This package additionally contains ONE modified file from Tidal-Media-Downloader
  https://github.com/yaronzz/Tidal-Media-Downloader
  Copyright (c) Yaronzz, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The original license is reproduced in LICENSE. Apache-2.0 section 4(b) requires
prominent notice of modifications; this file records them.

Vendored from TIDALDL-PY/tidal_dl @ f4854f4 into _vendor/:
  decryption.py   (itself originally from the RedSea project)

Modification: imports made relative. Upstream used flat, Python-2-style
imports that required the package directory itself to be on sys.path.

tidalapi resolves streams but does not decrypt them, which is why this one
file remains.

Why the rest was dropped
------------------------
The vendored tree originally covered auth, metadata, streaming, downloading and
tagging (tidal.py, download.py, model.py, paths.py, settings.py, enums.py,
apiKey.py, plus printf.py and lang/). All of it was removed in favour of
tidalapi after its hardcoded API keys proved to be revoked for playback.

Verified against one account and track, back to back:

  * yaronzz keys - device login succeeds, /v1/sessions returns 200, the
    subscription reports ACTIVE / PREMIUM / LOSSLESS / premiumAccess=true and
    the track reports allowStreaming=true, yet EVERY playbackinfo request
    returns 401 subStatus 4005 "Asset is not ready for playback" - at every
    quality, and on both the prepaywall and postpaywall endpoints.
    Key 4 (zU4XHVVkc2tDPo4t) is blocked by CloudFront at /token outright.
  * tidalapi credentials - same account, same track, same minute: LOSSLESS,
    HIGH and LOW all return a usable stream URL.

Tidal has revoked playback for those leaked 2023-era client ids while leaving
authentication working, which is why the failure looked like a hang rather than
an auth error. Upstream's last functional commit was October 2023, so nothing
there will be refreshed. Depending on a maintained library means credential
rotations arrive as an upgrade rather than a hand-patch.

Behaviour carried over deliberately
-----------------------------------
  * Quality.BEST walks MAX -> HIFI -> HIGH -> LOW and takes the highest rung
    the account and track actually serve. Availability is tier-dependent: a
    LOSSLESS-tier subscription returns 401 for MAX (HI_RES_LOSSLESS).
  * MQA / "Master" is never requested. This is now structural rather than
    guarded: tidalapi 0.8.x's Quality enum has no MQA member, where upstream
    defaulted to it whenever an AudioQuality member was unmapped.
  * poll_login() stays a single non-blocking check so a web request handler
    never blocks for the lifetime of a device code.
